In the case Raman signal is lost completely, follow this guide.
0. Check spectrometer is set to grating 3 and is in position (via Hg lamp), check camera is working (using Hg lamp). Check aser is on, and sample is in focus (not degraded). Check no laser blockers sit in the optical path.
0.5!!! PLACE A LASER BLOCKER AT THE VERY END OF THE OPTICAL PATH TO PREVENT DIRECT LASER CONTACT WITH CAMERA
1. Home gratings 1-4
2. Align g1 to fit through the pinhole placed in front of the sample (this is the only 100% consistent reference)
3. Push g1 such that it passes cutoff filter 1. This is done by getting g1 on the edge of the filter, and moving until it cannot be abserved on the filter (approx -608 steps from alignment)
4. Place a fluorescent target near the end of the optical path, align g2 such that the (now broad) laser spot sits at middle-height. If no laser spot is observed, move g3 negative until it passes the 2nd cutoff filter
5. Move g3 until it is completely blocked by the 2nd cutoff filter
6. Move g4 to approximately the same position, with flipped sign
7. Return g1 to alingment
8. Remove all laser blockers/targets
9. Begin recording spectra (30 second acq)
10. If no signal is observed, move g4 to  aprofoundly far off distance and scan slowly